What: /sys/class/rtc/rtcN/alarm_events
Date: November 2026
Contact: Q2 Navidrome developers
Description:
 Read-only, version1, non-consuming snapshot of changes/events for the user AIE
 timer, overflow flag, enabled/deadline, last expiry boottime nanoseconds and
 the driver-declared alarm wake IRQ (0 means unknown).
 Fields are protected by the RTC ops lock. Setting/changing AIE increments
 changes; only the user AIE callback increments events. Internal alarmtimer
 rtc_timers do not increment events. Counters saturate and overflow prevents
 maintenance-only attribution. Read never consumes irq_data, opens /dev/rtc,
 disables an alarm or replaces a user deadline. Bind an open sysfs descriptor
 to this device instance; rebind/deactivation is not a valid maintenance wake.
